    <TD align="left" valign="top" colspan="4" height="115"><b>Found wandering the Karanas as a child by Thornish Treefont, treant shaman, Thosguard was taken to a hidden forest were he was raised amongst the tree folk.  He was tuttered in the ways of karana, for the treants believe he was a gift from karana.  
When he matured , Thornish took him to surefall glade to begin his finaly training. Having been left in the hands of the Rangers of Surefall, he watched as Thornish disappeared back into the horizon.   Many months went buy until at last he had finished the training and been accepted as one of Lord Karanas warriors.
Thosguard left Surefall , and began the trip to the treant village in order to deliver the news of his success.  Upon entering the forest , he found the trees and mutilated bodies of his treant adopters  charred and lifeless.  As he stood amongst a darkness began to rise in him.  His rage boiled in his blood as the saddness began to drag his soul down.  He began to frantically search for Thornish, and he found his Father of so Long, Crusified to a large Red Oak.
Thornish had not died in vain.  Scratched in the Oak was a fraise,  " Nectromas  Inoruka" (Children of Innurok).  
Thosguard removed his father from the tree with some great effort and went to the old treants keepsake tree. Removing a old book from, he opened the book to a encantation he had only seen once, "The Treant Ritual of Pacing".  Moving to each fallen comrad he softly spoke the encantation.  Flowers began to grow from the treelike bodies,  leaves turned and grass regained there green.  A soft breeze  slowly flowed throught the hidden forest.   Thosguard new there was but one encantation he had left for the resting place of his family.  He slowly gathered his belongings ..slowly passing to kneel before each body on last time and flash a memory of past joys and walked to the edge of the forest, silently he muttered the incantation," I brother of the tree, now lie beyond pain and loss, in the land set asside for me by my ancestors, guid my children true in my absence..oh might Karana".  And with the final words the grove began to close up tell at last an entrance was no longer available. Mists began to swirl as Thosguard looked back one last time..."Rest well brothers, your journey has ended. You are called home".

One soletary tear ran down his cheak. Softly he mourned as the rage burned in him "But, my hunt has just began"............  with that he walked into the mist and the forest with his grove home disappeared ...sealed away from all for eternity.


(So begins the Adventurers of "THOSGUARD FOESBANE"</b></TD>
